ary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.4.beta3.official [06acfccf8] - broken\nv4.4.beta2.official [a013481b0] - worked fine\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.beta3 - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Mobile) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX 6600 (Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; 32.0.11027.2001) - AMD Ryzen 5 3600 6-Core Processor (12 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nOn upgrading my project to 4.4-beta3, I get the error \"Parser Error: 'Util' not defined in the current scope\" in one of my scripts. This did not occur in 4.4-beta2 or earlier.\n\nThe error occurs in my `ConfigManager` autoload, which is near the start of my load order. The class `Util`, is a script which simply has a `class_name Util`, and a number of `static func`s, for general use.\n\nMy only assumption is that some sort of complex load order issue is causing it to fail to find `Util` at the time of `ConfigManager`. Attempting to reproduce this for an MRP has so far eluded me, so it seems unlikely to be trivial. `Util` does have some functions which reference other classes, ex. at least one of them checks for `is BaseScene`, referencing my `BaseScene` class; which itself references other autoloads that are after the ConfigManager? But attempting a similar setup in a fresh project didn't reproduce, so I'm really not sure exactly what's causing this.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nUnknown; but something definitely regressed here. Will edit with steps if I manage to reproduce cleanly.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nWill edit with MRP if I manage to reproduce cleanly.","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","fol